<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.12.2: Writing an Inequality to Represent a Constraint</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00585</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.12.2: Writing an Inequality to Represent a Constraint</md:title>
    <md:uuid>36593400-6040-478f-9f31-8040a84c999a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>For questions 1 – 8, use the following scenario:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>The homeowner is worried about the work needed to maintain a grass lawn and flower beds, so she is now looking at some low-maintenance materials.</para>
  <para>She is considering a combination of the materials shown to cover the yard. Her budget is still $3,000.</para>
  <list>
    <item>artificial turf: $15 per square foot</item>
    <item>gravel: $3 per square foot</item>
  </list>
  <para>Here is a graph representing some constraints in this situation.</para>
  <figure><media alt="Graph of a line. Artificial turf, square feet. Gravel, square feet."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c3064de980b0b1f57af968a42dadcfc6565921a3"/></media></figure></blockquote>
<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> The graph shows a line going through \((500,100)\). In this situation, what does the point \((500,100)\) mean? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The cost of installing 500 square feet of gravel and 100 square feet of artificial turf is $3000.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write an equation that the line represents. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(3x + 15y = 3000\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What do the solutions to the equation mean? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The solutions are all combinations of square feet of gravel and artificial turf that would cost $3000 to install.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> The point \((600,200)\) is located to the right and above the line. Does that combination of turf and gravel meet the homeowner's constraints? Be prepared to show your reasoning. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>No. Answers may vary, but here is a sample. If she installs 600 square feet of gravel and 200 square feet of turf, the cost is \(3(600)+15(200)\), which is \(1800 + 3,000\) or \($4800\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Choose another point in the same region (to the right and above the line). Check if the combination meets the homeowner's constraints. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Answers may vary, but here is a sample. \((900,50)\). This combination would cost more than $3000 to install.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> The point \((200,100)\) is located to the left and below the line. Does that combination of turf and gravel meet the homeowner's constraints? Be prepared to show your reasoning. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Yes. Answers may vary, but here is a sample: \(3(200) + 15(100) = 2100\). This amount is less than $3000.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#7-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Choose another point in the same region (to the left and below the line). Check if the combination meets the homeowner's constraints. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Answers may vary, but here is a sample: \((600, 25)\). This combination would cost under $3000 to install.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#8-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write an inequality that represents the constraints in this situation. Explain what the solutions mean and show the solution region on the graph. </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Answers may vary, but here is a sample:</para>
  <para>\(3x + 15y\leq3000\). The solutions represent all possible combinations of square feet of gravel and turf that would cost no more than $3000 to install.</para>
  <figure><media alt="Graph of an inequality. Artificial turf, square feet. Gravel, square feet."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/fc673e4dfadd0122b72eab842c8991654ba6c3cf"/></media></figure></solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<!--Interaction End -->


